docs {
  # Consumption — water_warm with meter replacement

  Default unit is **WE 01** (Musterstraße 2-4), which carries the demo meter-
  replacement scenario: the warm-water meter was replaced on 2025-06-12, so
  the 2025 billing year has **two device segments** under the same
  `measuring_point_id`:

  1. Old device, deinstalled 2025-06-12, `replacement_reason: DeviceReplacement`.
  2. Replacement device, no deinstall date. Its `baseline_value` is its own
     start value at installation (`0.004`) — not necessarily 0.

  A range that starts after the replacement (e.g. 2026) shows only the
  replacement device.

  Each segment contains **one reading per calendar month end** (never finer;
  `is_synthetic: true` marks values messpunkt.io interpolated) and a
  `period_consumption` block. The number to bill is the sum of
  `period_consumption.billable_value` across both segments — do not compute
  it from the readings yourself. See the OpenAPI spec for the full contract.

  ## Query parameters

  - `from` — ISO-8601 date, inclusive; widened to the first day of its month
  - `to`   — ISO-8601 date, inclusive; widened to the last day of its month,
    capped at the last completed month
  - `metric` — one or more of `heat`, `hca`, `water_cold`, `water_warm`,
    `water_outdoor` (comma-separated)
}
